ent-WGLighthouseKeeper = the keeper
    .desc = A tidy old man in a heavy coat. He smiles a great deal.
ent-WGHospiceAttendant = hospice attendant
    .desc = Clean robes, gentle hands, a patient smile.
ent-WGHospiceCot = hospice cot
    .desc = White sheets, freshly turned. Lie down, and be mended.
ent-WGLastAnchorCore = the last anchor
    .desc = An anchor nobody built, flickering, failing, holding on.
ent-WGOrchardVine = flesh vine
    .desc = A rope of muscle and sinew, slowly reaching.
ent-WGOrchardRoot = vine root
    .desc = A knot of flesh where the vines begin.
ent-WGOrchardHanged = hanged body
    .desc = Hanging from the vines. It twitches when they move.
ent-WGGraveRock = grave rock
    .desc = A rock with letters scratched into it.
ent-WGWaitingBoard = number board
    .desc = NOW SERVING, in red, over a number.
ent-WGTicketDispenser = ticket dispenser
    .desc = Take a number. Someone has already taken yours.
ent-WGBroadcastTransmitter = transmitter mast
    .desc = A lattice mast with a red light. It is still broadcasting.

wg-codasite-lighthouse-beacon = Safe harbour. Safe harbour. The light is lit at bearing { $bearing }, { $km } kilometres out. All are welcome.
wg-codasite-keeper-line-1 = Seventy years I've kept this light. Not one night dark.
wg-codasite-keeper-line-2 = Rest. Nothing out there can reach you in here.
wg-codasite-keeper-line-3 = The others are below, sleeping. Best not wake them.
wg-codasite-keeper-line-4 = There's tea, if you'd like it. There's always tea.
wg-codasite-keeper-line-5 = You came in on the last tide. Didn't you?
wg-codasite-keeper-line-6 = I knew your face before you docked. I'm sure of it.
wg-codasite-keeper-line-7 = The light doesn't need oil any more. I don't ask why.
wg-codasite-keeper-line-8 = Stay as long as you like. Everyone does.
wg-codasite-keeper-asks = Have you seen { $name }? They were here a moment ago.
wg-codasite-keeper-woke = There you are. You slept so soundly.
wg-codasite-keeper-standing = The keeper is standing over you, smiling.
wg-codasite-hospice-healed = Every wound closes. Something else opens, somewhere behind your eyes.
wg-codasite-grave-name = Scratched into the stone: { $name }.
wg-codasite-grave-blank = The stone is smooth. Waiting for a name.
wg-codasite-grave-weight = As the stone breaks, { $name }'s weight settles on you.
wg-codasite-waiting-called = NOW SERVING: { $number }. That's your number.
wg-codasite-waiting-board = NOW SERVING: { $number }

cmd-wgcodasite-desc = Places the Coda sites, or says where they are.
cmd-wgcodasite-help = Usage: wgcodasite place|where
cmd-wgcodasite-at = {$site}: {$position}
cmd-wgcodasite-placed = {$site}: placed at {$position}
cmd-wgcodasite-no-place = {$site}: no clear place
cmd-wgcodasite-not-placed = {$site}: not placed

# Shared stone, glass and light.
ent-WGCodaStoneWall = carved stone wall
    .desc = Old stone, laid in lines that run on into the dark.
ent-WGCodaStainedGlass = stained glass
    .desc = Diamond panes of violet, crimson, teal and amber, held in lead.
ent-WGCodaWallTorch = wall torch
    .desc = An iron bracket holding a torch that never seems to burn down.
ent-WGCodaCandle = candle
    .desc = Someone lit it. Nobody remembers who.
ent-WGCodaBrazier = brazier
    .desc = A bowl of fire on iron legs. It gives off light, and very little warmth.
ent-WGCodaCandleStand = candle stand
    .desc = A tall iron stand with a single candle.
ent-WGCodaLanternPost = lantern post
    .desc = A lantern on a hook.
ent-WGCodaChains = hanging chains
    .desc = Rusted chains hanging from the dark.
ent-WGCodaBones = bones
    .desc = What's left of someone.
ent-WGCodaTombstone = tombstone
    .desc = A grave marker with the name worn off.
ent-WGCodaTombstoneCracked = cracked tombstone
    .desc = A split grave marker.
tiles-wg-coda-stone = worn stone
tiles-wg-coda-rough = rough stone
tiles-wg-coda-wood = herringbone wood

# The Echo Station.
ent-WGEchoFigure = echo
    .desc = A pale shape going through the motions. It doesn't seem to see you.
ent-WGEchoNewsBoard = noticeboard
    .desc = Yellowed notices, pinned up long ago.
ent-WGEchoAnchor = dead anchor
    .desc = A copy of Central's anchor, cold and still. Almost still.
wg-codasite-echo-line-1 = Dock three's clear. Bring her in slow.
wg-codasite-echo-line-2 = Shift change in ten. Same as yesterday.
wg-codasite-echo-line-3 = Your booking's for the fourteenth. You're early. Or late.
wg-codasite-echo-line-4 = Fuel's on the house today. It always is.
wg-codasite-echo-line-5 = The anchor's humming again. Nobody's worried.
wg-codasite-echo-line-6 = Lunch was good. I think it was good.
wg-codasite-echo-line-7 = Mind the wet floor. It's been wet a long time.
wg-codasite-echo-line-8 = Next, please. Next. Next.
wg-codasite-echo-line-9 = We're closing up soon. We've been closing up for years.
wg-codasite-echo-line-10 = Welcome to Caelestinus Central. Welcome. Welcome.
wg-codasite-echo-name = Has anyone seen { $name }? Their ship came in years ago.
wg-codasite-echo-news-blank = The notices have faded past reading.
wg-codasite-echo-news-heading = Among the faded notices:
wg-codasite-echo-news-line = LOST: { $name }. { $years } years ago. Still missed.
wg-codasite-echo-anchor-twitch = The dead anchor twitches.
wg-codasite-echo-crumbles = { CAPITALIZE(THE($item)) } crumbles to dust.

# What the Echo calls itself on scanners: never Central.
wg-codasite-echo-grid-name-1 = Afterimage
wg-codasite-echo-grid-name-2 = The Hollow Hour
wg-codasite-echo-grid-name-3 = Last Arrivals
wg-codasite-echo-grid-name-4 = Stillness
wg-codasite-echo-grid-name-5 = Remembrance Station

# The keeper's gift.
wg-codasite-keeper-gives = Here. Something warm, and a light for the dark out there. Go carefully.
wg-codasite-keeper-given = I've nothing more to give you. Go on, now.
wg-codasite-keeper-calm = The cup is warm. For a moment, your head is quiet.

# The Last Anchor, fed.
wg-codasite-anchor-fed = The core drinks it in. It steadies, for a while longer.

# The Hospice's mark.
wg-codasite-hospice-attendant-1 = There. All mended. You won't remember the pain.
wg-codasite-hospice-attendant-2 = Rest a moment. Everyone rests here, in the end.
wg-codasite-hospice-attendant-3 = Such a small price. You'll hardly notice it.
wg-codasite-hospice-attendant-4 = Come back whenever you're hurt. We'll always have a bed for you.
wg-codasite-hospice-whisper-1 = You smell antiseptic. Nobody else does.
wg-codasite-hospice-whisper-2 = Somewhere, a bed is still warm from you.
wg-codasite-hospice-whisper-3 = A kind voice says your name. Nobody is there.
wg-codasite-hospice-whisper-4 = Your wounds itch where they used to be.
wg-codasite-hospice-whisper-5 = You hear a heart monitor, slow and patient, in time with your own.
wg-codasite-hospice-marked = There is something too calm in their eyes, like they've been somewhere quiet.

# The Orchard's snare.
wg-codasite-orchard-snared = The vines wind round your legs while you stand still. Move!

# Tending a grave.
wg-codasite-grave-tended = You lay a stone for {$name}. Something in your head settles.
wg-codasite-grave-tended-already = You've already tended {$name}'s grave.

# The Waiting Room's figure.
wg-codasite-waiting-behind = Someone is standing right behind you.

# Speaking at the mast.
wg-codasite-tower-took = The mast hums as you speak. Your words have gone somewhere.
wg-codasite-waiting-ticket = A ticket slides out of the dispenser and into your hand. You don't remember taking it. Your number will be called.
